  "details": "Occasionally the 'lock head' option will lock your head's movement to your spine. Meaning when you turn your head, your upper chest will move with it.\n\nThis makes it so that your spine moves with all the 'lock positions', 'lock both' and 'lock hips' now move your neck with the chest.\n\nThis effectively breaks FBT.\n\nSteps to recreate:\n\nRecalibrate, occasionally this will happen\n\nIt's happened when I've first gotten on VRC, when I've come back to my PC, and there seems to be no fix for it once it happens. It will just randomly fix itself.\n\nI am using four trackers total. One for my head for continuous calibration, one worn on the hips and two for both feet. No chest tracker.\n\nI used to be able to switch between the lock poses to fix it, I can't do that anymore.",
